  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FeSL makes use of the XACML Hierarchical Resource Profile (HRP) - ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/2.0/access_control-xacml-2.0-hier-profile-spec-os.pdf"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/2.0/access_control-xacml-2.0-hier-profile-spec-os.pdf",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-hierarchical-v1-spec-cs-01-en.pdf"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://docs.oasis-open.org/xacml/3.0/xacml-3.0-hierarchical-v1-spec-cs-01-en.pdf",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is used in evaluation permissions of members of collections, particularly when evaluating the precedence of policies in a hierarchy of collections and resources.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FeSL uses the \"URI path\" variant of this (as opposed to parent and ancestor attributes).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The XACML specification states that the resource-id used in the path to the resource (in the request context, and in the policy) MUST be a URI.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However FeSL specifies resource-id attribute values as (for example, individual path components are PIDs):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "/ns:TopCollection/ns:SubCollection/ns:someResource",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "... which is not a URI",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It could form the \"path\" component if a suitable URI scheme was chosen for this hierarchical resource-id within FeSL.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
  "duedate": null,
  "environment": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FeSL AuthZ enabled",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
