      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Interestingly the 3.0 spec states (2.2, lines 221 et seq)</p>\n\n<p>File system resources SHALL use the “file:” scheme. If the resource is identified with a standard &lt;scheme&gt; specified in <span class=\"error\">&#91;RFC3986&#93;</span> or in a related standard for a registered URI scheme which is hierarchical with slashes, then that scheme SHALL be used. Otherwise the URI SHALL use the “file:” scheme.</p>\n\n<p>This seems to suggest that if the resource does use an existing URI scheme <b>and</b> that scheme is hierarchical, that should be used.  Otherwise use \"file:\".</p>",
     "created": "01/Feb/11 7:44 PM",
